1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A complete guided tour with Urdu narration and English instructional captions.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,184
A local-first workspace for a pharmacy. Start with the guided setup.

3
00:00:12,184 --> 00:00:18,368
Add your store name, contact number and address for your workspace.

4
00:00:18,368 --> 00:00:24,552
Choose an Owner account and a strong password. Keep it private.

5
00:00:24,552 --> 00:00:30,736
Check the local currency and review your workspace preferences.

6
00:00:30,736 --> 00:00:37,920
Use your new account. Your business records stay on this computer.

7
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:46,850
Use the persistent sidebar to move between daily tasks.

8
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:55,780
Sales, stock alerts, receivables and recent activity appear here.

9
00:00:55,780 --> 00:01:04,710
Press Ctrl+K to search products and jump to workspace sections.

10
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:14,640
Open Help for POS shortcuts and a quick reference to core actions.

11
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:20,920
Open Suppliers to build the contact directory for your purchases.

12
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:27,200
Enter a fictional training supplier and save its contact information.

13
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:33,480
The supplier directory makes the same contact reusable on purchases.

14
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:39,760
Record the medicine name, category, SKU, barcode and prices.

15
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:46,040
A new product starts with zero units until stock is received.

16
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:53,320
Search the catalog and review prices, identifiers and stock levels.

17
00:01:53,320 --> 00:02:01,890
Receive stock against a supplier instead of changing quantities by hand.

18
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:10,460
Select a product, batch number, expiry, quantity, cost and selling price.

19
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:19,030
Check totals and amount paid before confirming the purchase.

20
00:02:19,030 --> 00:02:28,600
A confirmed purchase records the invoice and increases batch stock.

21
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:37,290
Review available units, reorder levels, stock value and nearest expiry.

22
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:45,980
Each batch keeps its own expiry, quantity and purchase cost.

23
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:54,670
The Expiring soon tab helps you identify products needing attention.

24
00:02:54,670 --> 00:03:04,360
Movements show when stock entered or left the store.

25
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:13,530
The POS groups product search, cart and bill summary on one screen.

26
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:22,700
Find the exact item by name, SKU or barcode; F2 focuses search.

27
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:31,870
Check quantity, total and received amount before completing the sale.

28
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:42,040
After checkout, open or print the sale receipt and start another sale.

29
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:47,446
Create a customer profile and, if needed, set a credit limit.

30
00:03:47,446 --> 00:03:52,851
Choose the customer, enter a partial payment and review the balance due.

31
00:03:52,851 --> 00:03:58,257
Sales history keeps invoice, customer, total, balance and return actions.

32
00:03:58,257 --> 00:04:03,663
Select the item and quantity; a return updates stock and credit together.

33
00:04:03,663 --> 00:04:09,069
The customer directory shows the remaining outstanding amount.

34
00:04:09,069 --> 00:04:14,474
Enter the amount collected to reduce an outstanding customer balance.

35
00:04:14,474 --> 00:04:20,880
The demo customer now has a zero outstanding balance.

36
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:30,610
Choose a category, date, description, amount and payment method.

37
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:40,340
Saved expenses appear in a searchable list and feed the finance view.

38
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:50,070
Revenue less cost of goods sold and expenses gives estimated net profit.

39
00:04:50,070 --> 00:05:00,800
Finance separates customer receivables from unpaid supplier invoices.

40
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:09,680
Select a report and date range to review recorded activity.

41
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:18,560
Use Export CSV to work with report data outside the app.

42
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:27,440
Stock reports help compare product quantities and inventory value.

43
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:37,320
Expiry reports identify batches that need prompt attention.

44
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:43,420
The Owner can review users and create accounts for staff.

45
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:49,520
Give each staff member their own credentials and appropriate role.

46
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:55,620
Review profile details, preferences and the local demo-data tools.

47
00:05:55,620 --> 00:06:01,720
Click Backup now, then keep another copy on a separate drive.

48
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:07,820
An Owner must confirm a restore; a safety backup is made first.

49
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:13,920
Keyboard shortcuts and workflow guidance remain available in Help.

50
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:20,920
Use fictional data for practice, then start with your own records and regular backups.
